# Title: LSASS Dump Keyword In CommandLine
# ID: ffa6861c-4461-4f59-8a41-578c39f3f23e
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: E.M. Anhaus, Tony Lambert, oscd.community, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2019-10-24
# Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.001
# Description: Detects the presence of the keywords "lsass" and ".dmp" in the commandline, which could indicate a potential attempt to dump or create a dump of the lsass process.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*lsass.dmp*" OR process_exec="*lsass.zip*" OR process_exec="*lsass.rar*" OR process_exec="*Andrew.dmp*" OR process_exec="*Coredump.dmp*" OR process_exec="*NotLSASS.zip*" OR process_exec="*lsass_2*" OR process_exec="*lsassdump*" OR process_exec="*lsassdmp*")) OR ((process_exec="*lsass*" AND process_exec="*.dmp*")) OR ((process_exec="*SQLDmpr*" AND process_exec="*.mdmp*")) OR ((process_exec="*nanodump*" AND process_exec="*.dmp*")))
